{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Zend Framework 1 End-of-Life{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">Zend Framework</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">Zend Framework 1 End-of-Life</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container py-4">
        <div class="row g-4">
            
            {% include '@partial/left-menu.html.twig' %}

            <main class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-9">
                <article class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5 h-100">
                    <header class="mb-4">
                        <h1 class="h2 text-dark fw-bold">Zend Framework 1 End-of-Life</h1>
                        <div class="text-muted small">
                            <i class="bi bi-folder2-open me-1"></i> Zend Framework
                        </div>
                    </header>

                    <section class="post-content text-secondary lh-lg fs-6">
                        EOL ( End-of-Life)  term  was just announced.

Only up until Sept. 28,2016 , Zend Framework 1 will receive security updates.

 

" With the release of Zend Framework 3, it's time to halt development on Zend Framework 1. As such, we hereby announce that Zend Framework 1 reaches its End of Life (EOL) three months from today, on 28 September 2016. "

 

Read the official <a href="https://framework.zend.com/blog/2016-06-28-zf1-eol.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">announcement .</a>
                    </section>
                </article>
            </main>
            
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}